#: docs/tablet-protocol.rst:64
msgid ""
"It describes the terminal on the system it runs on, not the hardware attached right now. A bit is"
" set only for what the terminal knows it can report. Where the system does not say beforehand "
"whether it gives the shape of a contact, bit ``8`` stays clear until a contact has had one, so a "
"program does not wait for the bit: a report has a shape when its ``valid`` says so. What goes "
"beyond tools and fingers, the bits from ``16`` up, is sent only when asked for with the mode. "
"``mode`` is the current state of the mode described below. ``w,h`` are the size of the cell area "
"in pixels (1 to 65535) and ``cw,ch`` the cell size (1 to 4096). Pixels, here and in the reports, "
"are physical pixels: those of the framebuffer the terminal draws into, not the scaled units of "
"the window system, so a position is as fine as the display is. A program queries again after a "
"resize. A terminal that does not support the protocol ignores the query, so a program must time "
"out and fall back to mouse reporting. A query does not change the mode."
msgstr ""
"能力位描述终端在所运行系统上能报告什么，而非当前连接了什么硬件。只有终端确定能报告的能力才设置相应位。如果系统不预先说明是否提供接触形状，则位 ``8`` "
"在实际出现带形状的接触前保持清除；程序不应等待该位，只要报告的 ``valid`` 声明存在，就应使用形状信息。超出工具和手指范围的能力（``16`` "
"及以上的位）只有通过模式请求后才发送。``mode`` 为下述模式的当前状态。``w,h`` 是字符单元区域的像素尺寸（1 至 65535），``cw,ch`` 为字符单元尺寸（1 至 "
"4096）。此处及报告中的像素均为终端帧缓冲区的物理像素，而非窗口系统缩放后的逻辑单位，因此位置精度与显示器一致。调整窗口大小后程序应重新查询。不支持本协议的终端会忽略查询，程序必须设置超时并回退到鼠标报告。查询不改变模式。"

