#: docs/tablet-protocol.rst:99
msgid ""
"While bit ``1`` or ``2`` is on, that kind of input over the window is reported with this protocol"
" instead of as mouse events, so with ``mode=1`` a pen draws while a finger still taps and scrolls"
" as a mouse, and with ``mode=3`` a tap is not a click and a drag does not select. A physical "
"mouse, and the mouse and scroll events a touchpad produces by itself, continue to use whatever "
"mouse reporting the program asked for. Programs that merely want pen input to act as a mouse need"
" not use the protocol at all. Bit ``4`` takes nothing away: what the system itself does with the "
"controls of a pad, such as a shortcut the user has put on a key, goes on."
msgstr ""
"开启位 ``1`` 或 ``2`` 时，窗口内对应输入通过本协议报告，不再作为鼠标事件。因此 ``mode=1`` 可用笔绘图，手指仍作为鼠标点击和滚动；``mode=3`` "
"下，轻点不再点击，拖动不再选择。物理鼠标，以及触控板自行产生的鼠标和滚动事件，仍使用程序请求的鼠标报告方式。只希望笔作为鼠标使用的程序无须使用本协议。位 ``4`` "
"不会剥夺既有功能：系统对控制板控件的操作，例如用户绑定到某个按键的快捷键，仍会执行。"

#: docs/tablet-protocol.rst:109
msgid ""
"The mode is local to the window, is reset by ``RIS``, and changing it cancels every active "
"contact and lets go of every held key of a pad. Programs must turn it off when they exit, suspend"
" or fail, and turn it back on when resumed. Multiplexers keep it with the rest of the terminal "
"state, restore it on reconnect, and turn it off when detaching. A terminal may let its user "
"refuse a mode, or some of its bits, for every program or for some. A refused bit reads back as "
"off and nothing it would have turned on is reported. kitty refuses bit ``8``, the hardware "
"identifiers, unless its user allows them with :opt:`tablet_hardware_ids`, since a serial number "
"says whose pen it is and the program asking may be on another machine. A refusal shows in the "
"mode, not in ``caps``, which says what the terminal can report on the system it runs on."
msgstr ""
"模式仅作用于当前窗口，由 ``RIS`` "
"重置；改变模式会取消所有活动接触，并释放控制板上所有按住的按键。程序必须在退出、挂起或失败时关闭，恢复时重新开启。多路复用器与其他状态一起保存它，重连时恢复，脱离连接时关闭。终端可允许用户针对全部或部分程序拒绝模式或某些位；被拒绝的位读回为关闭，不发送其本应启用的报告。kitty"
" 默认拒绝硬件标识位 ``8``，除非用户通过 :opt:`tablet_hardware_ids` 允许，因为序列号可识别笔的所有者，查询程序可能运行在远程机器上。拒绝体现在模式中，而非 "
"``caps``；后者描述终端在该系统上具有的报告能力。"

#: docs/tablet-protocol.rst:122
msgid ""
"A ``mode`` request without a ``mode`` field reads the state instead of changing it, and is "
